  "visualBrief": "Dated2012–2014Chinese Theatre: retained native rear auditorium/curved open forecourt with paired south street gateway blocks/faceted bronze spires and CHINESEblades. One swept hipped green-bronze pagoda roof/short ridge/trident finials/upturned bladed corners; tall coral square posts with original geometric open-mouth wrought masks/tusks/looped whiskers. Stepped pale corbels/coral gold panels, deep grid-ceiling portico/round gong/stone dragon panel/separate small canopy/sun disk, golden paired doors with tiny pagoda slot frames and pale seated guardian lions. Lower grid-window wings/curved red band, court piers/niches/abstract flame+bell plaques; neutral blank marquees. Native ground unchanged/graded paving, no handprint microdetail/ad artwork/photo pixels/modern neighbors/interior.",
